  "invariants": [
    "Use the existing EventDispatcher, textarea/select default hooks and original wheel manager; do not add page event listeners or a second native wheel default.",
    "Only the staged original trusted WheelEvent can reach the real shared native wheel API. Explicit page cancellation and nested synthetic events retain original behavior.",
    "Capture semantic node/control identity before page callbacks. If retired, complete that old native target default without accessing its freed control. Return original DispatchEventResult value 2; the original manager converts it to its acknowledgement.",
    "All wheel distances, bounds, selection, clipping and images remain owned by the unchanged real GNUstep controls. No animation implementation is copied; failed cancellation/takeover prototypes remain only in evidence.",
    "Toolbar, address bar and tabs keep browser components. Later GTK/Qt/KDE consumers reuse the shared provider/bridge with optional app-specific patches."
  ]
